# Keep derived data out of the bind-mounted workspace.
#
# Files a container creates under /workspaces are owned by whoever created them
# and come out mode 0755, so a cache written by root makes every later run as
# `vscode` fail with "Permission denied" -- and the Windows host cannot fix the
# ownership. Caches are per-container throwaway data, so the cure is to write
# them outside the mount entirely.
#
# Used twice: by the devcontainer service (env_file in docker-compose.yml) and
# by the throwaway verification containers in CLAUDE.md, which run as root.
# Paths are deliberately container-internal, so they work under any user.
PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=/tmp/cv-generator/pycache
MYPY_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/cv-generator/mypy
RUFF_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/cv-generator/ruff
PYTEST_ADDOPTS=-o cache_dir=/tmp/cv-generator/pytest
